# Contact form delivery. Without this the form reports that it is unavailable
# and points visitors at the email address directly.
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# Guestbook and visitor-counter storage.
#
# The guestbook and the hit counter are shared between visitors, so they need
# somewhere real to live. Any Postgres works: the free tier of Neon or
# Supabase, or a database on a box you own. Nothing here ties the site to its
# host. Both tables are created on first use.
#
# Use the POOLED connection string, not the direct one. Serverless runs many
# short-lived instances and pointing them all at a direct connection exhausts
# the server's connection limit; both Neon and Supabase hand out a pooler URL
# for exactly this. On Supabase it is the one on port 6543.
#
# The table is created on first use, so there is no migration to run.
#
# With this unset the guestbook falls back to an in-process list so local
# development works out of the box. That list is per-instance and does not
# survive a restart, and on serverless each instance has its own, so entries
# will not be shared. The window says as much when it is running that way.
DATABASE_URL=

# Guestbook moderation.
#
# The guestbook shows writing from anyone on the internet, so the owner needs
# a way to take an entry down. Set this to any long random string and the
# guestbook window offers a Moderate button that asks for it; entering it
# reveals a Delete button on every entry.
#
# The key is read on the server only and never reaches the browser: the
# window sends it back with each delete to be checked again. Wrong guesses
# are rate limited to five per ten minutes per address.
#
# With this unset there is no moderation at all, and the button is not drawn.
GUESTBOOK_ADMIN_KEY=
